# Cached external graphs.
#
# What is re-derivable is not committed; what is not, is.
#
# `fetch-external.py` re-fetches every row in `manifest.md`, and the
# manifest records each payload's SHA-256 — so a checkout can rebuild
# the cache and prove byte-identity with what was audited. Committing
# 4 MB of qudt-units.ttl to assert what a hash already asserts is the
# copy-of-a-copy defect this project keeps closing.
#
# The exceptions are the graphs that CANNOT be re-fetched from here:
# `schema.knowwheregraph.org` does not resolve and the UCSB host's
# certificate has expired, so the DEO and UNDRR-HIP files were supplied
# by hand. Losing them on a clean checkout would lose the only copy.
graphs/*.ttl

!graphs/disaster-event-module-generalized.ttl
!graphs/disaster-event-module-extensions.ttl
!graphs/disaster-properties-ontology.ttl
!graphs/undrr-isc-hazard-classification.ttl
